WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.880
- Mr. Carling, I have the conn.
- Captain has the conn.

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:06.924
- Right standard rudder at 0-7-9.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:10.177
- Right standard rudder to 0-7-9.
Aye-aye, sir.

00:00:10.886 --> 00:00:15.265
- All escorts, Greyhound.
Return to your stations immediately.

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:18.519
We have enemy contact, bearing 0-8-7.

00:00:23.607 --> 00:00:29.071
- Just imagine any way a sheep
would try to escape a pack of wolves,

00:00:29.154 --> 00:00:32.866
and you've got a ship trying to
get away from the Nazi submarines.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.661
That was the game of
The Battle of the Atlantic.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.415
- A wolf pack shadowing us.

00:00:40.499 --> 00:00:42.251
- They'll attack as a group.

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:43.877
- Yeah, waiting for nightfall.

00:00:43.961 --> 00:00:47.089
- "Greyhound" is about
an American destroyer

00:00:47.172 --> 00:00:51.426
escorting a convoy of merchant vessels
that's crossing the Atlantic

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.513
to bring vital war material
and soldiers to our allies.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:58.225
- Captain Krause has been
given quite a lot of responsibility

00:00:58.308 --> 00:01:02.020
as a first time commander.
It's a bit of a trial by fire.

00:01:02.104 --> 00:01:03.146
- Hard right rudder!
Hard over!

00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:08.443
- The Nazis had submarines, U-boats,

00:01:08.527 --> 00:01:13.866
and their job was to sink any allied ship
that was floating at sea.

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:19.663
(sonar pinging)

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:21.206
- That dead silence...

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:22.916
(sonar pinging)

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.128
...and just waiting to see
what's on your radar screen.

00:01:26.211 --> 00:01:27.171
(sonar pinging)

00:01:27.254 --> 00:01:31.300
You can imagine how it must've felt for
the men back then, coming under attack.

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:33.927
- He's trying to slip under us!

00:01:34.011 --> 00:01:35.721
- All mounts, fire at will.

00:01:38.557 --> 00:01:41.518
- We're nowhere near air cover,
we're low on fuel.

00:01:41.602 --> 00:01:44.771
No one has any idea
if they are going to make it.

00:01:44.855 --> 00:01:46.106
- U-boat, starboard bow!

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:51.987
- What you did yesterday...
got us to today.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:55.324
- It's not enough, Charlie.
Not nearly enough.

00:01:56.158 --> 00:02:00.829
- Krause has a lot of pressure on himself
'cause he has a lot of lives at his hands,

00:02:00.913 --> 00:02:04.750
and every decision he makes determines
the outcome of the whole crew.

00:02:06.335 --> 00:02:09.171
- I don't think there's any commander
that doesn't have

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:11.882
this innate fear of being wrong.

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:15.135
But that has to be conquered.
You cannot let your command

00:02:15.219 --> 00:02:18.138
be governed by this nagging doubt
of, "What if I am wrong?"

00:02:18.222 --> 00:02:19.306
- Here they come.

00:02:20.641 --> 00:02:24.853
- The goods will be
delivered by this nation,

00:02:24.937 --> 00:02:29.066
whose Navy believes
in the tradition of,

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:32.236
"Damn the torpedoes,
full speed ahead."

00:02:32.319 --> 00:02:34.780
- All hands, brace for collision!

